#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr ""
"Un curso gratuito de IBM sobre información cuántica y computación cuántica"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulations of measurements"
msgstr "Formulaciones matemáticas de las mediciones"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The lesson begins with two equivalent mathematical descriptions of "
"measurements:\n"
msgstr ""
"La lección comienza con dos descripciones matemáticas equivalentes de las "
"mediciones:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"General measurements can be described by *collections of matrices*, one for "
"each measurement outcome, in a way that generalizes the description of "
"projective measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las mediciones generales pueden describirse mediante *colecciones de "
"matrices* — una para cada resultado de medición — que generalizan la "
"descripción de las mediciones proyectivas.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"General measurements can be described as *channels* whose outputs are always"
" classical states (represented by diagonal density matrices).\n"
msgstr ""
"Las mediciones generales pueden describirse como *canales* cuyas salidas son"
" siempre estados clásicos (representados por matrices de densidad "
"diagonales).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll restrict our attention to measurements having *finitely many* possible outcomes.\n"
"Although it is possible to define measurements with infinitely many possible outcomes, they're much less typically encountered in the context of computation and information processing, and they also require some additional mathematics (namely measure theory) to be properly formalized.\n"
msgstr ""
"Restringimos nuestra consideración a mediciones con un número *finito* de resultados posibles.\n"
"Si bien es posible definir mediciones con infinitos resultados posibles, estas surgen con mucha menos frecuencia en el contexto de la computación y el procesamiento de información; ademas, requieren matemáticas adicionales (concretamente, teoría de la medida) para formalizarlas adecuadamente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our initial focus will be on so-called *destructive* measurements, where the output of the measurement is a classical measurement outcome alone — with no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of whatever system was measured.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, we can imagine that such a measurement destroys the quantum system itself, or that the system is immediately discarded once the measurement is made.\n"
"Later in the lesson we'll broaden our view and consider *non-destructive* measurements, where there's both a classical measurement outcome and a post-measurement quantum state of the measured system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inicialmente nos centramos en las llamadas mediciones *destructivas*, en las que el resultado de la medición es únicamente el valor clásico medido — sin especificación del estado post-medición del sistema medido.\n"
"Intuitivamente, podemos imaginar que dicha medición destruye el sistema cuántico en si, o que el sistema se descarta inmediatamente después de la medición.\n"
"Más adelante en la lección, ampliamos nuestra consideración a las mediciones *no destructivas*, en las que hay tanto un resultado clásico de medición como un estado post-medición del sistema medido.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurements as collections of matrices {#measurements-as-collections-of-"
"matrices}"
msgstr ""
"Mediciones como colecciones de matrices {#measurements-as-collections-of-"
"matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system that is to be measured, and assume for simplicity that the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ for some positive integer $n,$ so that density matrices representing quantum states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are $n\\times n$ matrices.\n"
"We won't actually have much need to refer to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X},$ but it will be convenient to refer to $n,$ the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"We'll also assume that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sea $\\mathsf{X}$ un sistema a medir, y supongamos por simplicidad que el conjunto de estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ es $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ para un entero positivo $n$, de modo que las matrices de densidad que describen estados cuánticos de $\\mathsf{X}$ son matrices $n\\times n$.\n"
"Raramente necesitaremos referirnos a los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$, pero resulta conveniente hacer referencia a $n$, el número de estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Suponemos ademas que los posibles resultados de la medición son los enteros $0,\\ldots,m-1$ para un entero positivo $m$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that we're just using these names to keep things simple;\n"
"it's straightforward to generalize everything that follows to other finite sets of classical states and measurement outcomes, renaming them as desired.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estos nombres son meramente por conveniencia; todo lo que sigue se "
"generaliza fácilmente a otros conjuntos finitos de estados clásicos y "
"resultados de medición renombrandolos apropiadamente.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Mediciones proyectivas {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that a *projective measurement* is described by a collection of *projection matrices* that sum to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols,\n"
msgstr ""
"Una *medición proyectiva* se describe mediante una colección de *matrices de proyección* que suman la matriz identidad.\n"
"En símbolos:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"describes a projective measurement of $\\mathsf{X}$ if each $\\Pi_a$ is an "
"$n\\times n$ projection matrix and the following condition is met.\n"
msgstr ""
"describe una medición proyectiva de $\\mathsf{X}$ si cada $\\Pi_a$ es una "
"matriz de proyección $n\\times n$ y se satisface la siguiente condición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it's in a state described by some quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ each outcome $a$ is obtained with probability equal to $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.$\n"
"We also have that the post-measurement state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is obtained by normalizing the vector $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ but we're ignoring the post-measurement state for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando dicha medición se realiza sobre un sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ que se encuentra en el estado $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, cada resultado $a$ ocurre con probabilidad $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2$.\n"
"El estado post-medición de $\\mathsf{X}$ se obtiene normalizando el vector $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, que por ahora ignoramos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ "
"rather than a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ then we can "
"alternatively express the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ as "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando el estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ se describe mediante una matriz de "
"densidad $\\rho$ en lugar de un vector de estado cuántico "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, la probabilidad del resultado $a$ puede expresarse "
"alternativamente como $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is a pure state, then "
"the two expressions are equal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Si $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ es un estado puro, las "
"dos expresiones son iguales:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're using the cyclic property of the trace for the second equality, "
"and for the third equality we're using the fact that each $\\Pi_a$ is a "
"projection matrix, and therefore satisfies $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí usamos la propiedad cíclica de la traza para la segunda igualdad y el "
"hecho de que cada $\\Pi_a$ es una matriz de proyección y por tanto satisface"
" $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a$ para la tercera igualdad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if $\\rho$ is a convex combination\n"
msgstr "Si $\\rho$ es en general una combinación convexa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"of pure states, then the expression $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ "
"coincides with the average probability for the outcome $a,$ owing to the "
"fact that this expression is linear in $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"de estados puros, entonces la expresión $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ "
"coincide con la probabilidad promedio del resultado $a$, ya que esta "
"expresión es lineal en $\\rho$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements {#general-measurements}"
msgstr "Mediciones generales {#general-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mathematical description for general measurements is obtained by relaxing the definition of projective measurements.\n"
"Specifically, we allow the matrices in the collection describing the measurement to be arbitrary *positive semidefinite* matrices rather than projections.\n"
"(Projections are always positive semidefinite; they can alternatively be defined as positive semidefinite matrices whose eigenvalues are all either 0 or 1.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Una descripción matemática de las mediciones generales se obtiene relajando la definición de mediciones proyectivas.\n"
"Concretamente, permitimos que las matrices en la colección que describe la medición sean matrices *positivas semidefinidas* arbitrarias en lugar de proyecciones.\n"
"(Las proyecciones son siempre positivas semidefinidas; pueden definirse alternativamente como matrices positivas semidefinidas con valores propios exclusivamente en $\\{0, 1\\}$.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, a general measurement of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ having "
"outcomes $0,\\ldots,m-1$ is specified by a collection of positive "
"semidefinite matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ whose rows and columns "
"correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and that meet the "
"condition\n"
msgstr ""
"Una medición general de un sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ con resultados "
"$0,\\ldots,m-1$ se especifica entonces mediante una colección de matrices "
"positivas semidefinidas $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ cuyas filas y columnas "
"corresponden a los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ y que satisfacen la "
"condición\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured while it is in a state described by the density matrix $\\rho,$ then each outcome\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ appears with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando el sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ en el estado $\\rho$ se mide, cada resultado\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ ocurre con probabilidad $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As we must naturally demand, the vector of outcome probabilities\n"
msgstr ""
"Como naturalmente debemos exigir, el vector de probabilidades de los "
"resultados\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"of a general measurement always forms a probability vector, for any choice of a density matrix $\\rho.$\n"
"The following two observations establish that this is the case.\n"
msgstr ""
"de una medición general siempre forma un vector de probabilidad, para cualquier matriz de densidad $\\rho$.\n"
"Las siguientes dos observaciones muestran que esto es efectivamente así.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each value $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ must be nonnegative, owing to the"
" fact that the trace of the product of any two positive semidefinite "
"matrices is always nonnegative:\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada valor $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ es no negativo, ya que la traza "
"del producto de dos matrices positivas semidefinidas cualesquiera es siempre"
" no negativa:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   One way to argue this fact is to use spectral decompositions of $Q$ and "
"$R$ together with the cyclic property of the trace to express the trace of "
"the product $QR$ as a sum of nonnegative real numbers, which must therefore "
"be nonnegative.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Esto puede demostrarse, por ejemplo, utilizando las descomposiciones "
"espectrales de $Q$ y $R$ junto con la propiedad cíclica de la traza: se "
"expresa la traza del producto $QR$ como una suma de números reales no "
"negativos, que por tanto debe ser no negativa.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The condition $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ together"
" with the linearity of the trace ensures that the probabilities sum to "
"$1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"La condición $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ junto con"
" la linealidad de la traza asegura que las probabilidades suman $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 1: any projective measurement {#example-1-any-projective-"
"measurement}"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplo 1: Cualquier medición proyectiva {#example-1-any-projective-"
"measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Projections are always positive semidefinite, so every projective "
"measurement is an example of a general measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las proyecciones son siempre positivas semidefinidas, por lo que cualquier "
"medición proyectiva es un ejemplo de medición general.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, a standard basis measurement of a qubit can be represented by "
"$\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Una medición en la base estándar de un qubit puede representarse, por "
"ejemplo, mediante $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$, donde\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measuring a qubit in the state $\\rho$ results in outcome probabilities as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"La medición de un qubit en el estado $\\rho$ produce las siguientes "
"probabilidades de resultado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 2: a non-projective qubit measurement {#example-2-a-non-projective-"
"qubit-measurement}"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplo 2: Una medición no proyectiva de qubit {#example-2-a-non-projective-"
"qubit-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a qubit, and define two matrices as follows.\n"
msgstr "Sea $\\mathsf{X}$ un qubit, y definamos dos matrices como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These are both positive semidefinite matrices: they're Hermitian, and in both cases the eigenvalues happen to be $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6,$ which are both positive.\n"
"We also have that $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I},$ and therefore $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ describes a measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ambas matrices son positivas semidefinidas: son hermíticas, y sus valores propios en ambos casos son $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6$, que son ambos positivos.\n"
"Ademas se cumple $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I}$, por lo que $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ describe una medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ and we perform this measurement, then the probability of obtaining the outcome $0$ is $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ and the probability of obtaining the outcome $1$ is\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho).$\n"
"For instance, if $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ then the probabilities for the two outcomes $0$ and $1$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando el sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ en el estado $\\rho$ se mide con esta medición, la probabilidad del resultado $0$ es $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ y la del resultado $1$ es $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)$.\n"
"Si, por ejemplo, $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$, las probabilidades de los resultados $0$ y $1$ son las siguientes:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 3: tetrahedral measurement {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"
msgstr "Ejemplo 3: Medición tetraédrica {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define four single-qubit quantum state vectors as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Definamos cuatro vectores de estado cuántico de un solo qubit como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These four states are sometimes known as *tetrahedral* states because "
"they're vertices of a *regular tetrahedron* inscribed within the Bloch "
"sphere.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estos cuatro estados a veces se denominan *estados tetraédricos*, ya que "
"forman los vertices de un *tetraedro regular* inscrito en la esfera de "
"Bloch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Illustration of a tetrahedron inscribed in the Bloch "
"sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Ilustración de un tetraedro inscrito en la esfera de "
"Bloch](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Cartesian coordinates of these four states on the Bloch sphere are\n"
msgstr ""
"Las coordenadas cartesianas de estos cuatro estados en la esfera de Bloch "
"son\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which can be verified by expressing the density matrices representations of "
"these states as linear combinations of Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"lo cual puede verificarse expresando las representaciones como matrices de "
"densidad de estos estados como combinaciones lineales de matrices de "
"Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These four states are perfectly spread out on the Bloch sphere, each one "
"equidistant from the other three and with the angles between any two of them"
" always being the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estos cuatro estados están distribuidos uniformemente en la esfera de Bloch:"
" cada estado tiene la misma distancia a los otros tres, y los ángulos entre "
"cualesquiera dos estados son siempre iguales.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let us define a measurement $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ of a qubit by "
"setting $P_a$ as follows for each $a=0,\\ldots,3.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora definimos una medición $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ de un qubit "
"estableciendo $P_a$ para cada $a=0,\\ldots,3$ como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can verify that this is a valid measurement as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Que esto es una medición válida puede verificarse de la siguiente manera.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each $P_a$ is evidently positive semidefinite, being a pure state divided by one-half.\n"
"That is, each one is a Hermitian matrix and has one eigenvalue equal to $1/2$ and all other eigenvalues zero.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada $P_a$ es obviamente positiva semidefinida, ya que es un estado puro dividido por dos.\n"
"Es decir, cada $P_a$ es una matriz hermítica con un valor propio $1/2$ y todos los demás valores propios iguales a cero.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sum of these matrices is the identity matrix: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"The expressions of these matrices as linear combinations of Pauli matrices makes this straightforward to verify.\n"
msgstr ""
"La suma de estas matrices es la matriz identidad: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}$.\n"
"Esto puede verificarse fácilmente usando las representaciones de estas matrices como combinaciones lineales de matrices de Pauli.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Measurements as channels {#measurements-as-channels}"
msgstr "Mediciones como canales {#measurements-as-channels}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A second way to describe measurements in mathematical terms is as "
"channels.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una segunda forma de describir las mediciones matemáticamente consiste en "
"concebirlas como canales.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Classical information can be viewed as a special case of quantum information, insofar as we can identify probabilistic states with diagonal density matrices.\n"
"So, in operational terms, we can think about measurements as being channels whose inputs are matrices describing states of whatever system is being measured and whose outputs are *diagonal* density matrices describing the resulting distribution of measurement outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"La información clásica puede considerarse como un caso especial de la información cuántica, identificando los estados probabilísticos con matrices de densidad diagonales.\n"
"Operativamente, podemos por tanto entender las mediciones como canales cuyas entradas son matrices que describen estados del sistema medido y cuyas salidas son matrices de densidad *diagonales* que describen la distribución resultante de los resultados de medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll see shortly that any channel having this property can always be written in a simple, canonical form that ties directly to the description of measurements as collections of positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"Conversely, given an arbitrary measurement as a collection of matrices, there's always a valid channel having the diagonal output property that describes the given measurement as suggested in the previous paragraph.\n"
"Putting these observations together, we find that the two descriptions of general measurements are equivalent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Veremos enseguida que cualquier canal con esta propiedad siempre puede escribirse en una forma simple y canónica que se relaciona directamente con la descripción de mediciones como colecciones de matrices positivas semidefinidas.\n"
"Recíprocamente, para cualquier medición dada como colección de matrices, siempre existe un canal válido con la propiedad de salida diagonal que describe la medición dada según el párrafo anterior.\n"
"De estas observaciones se deduce que las dos descripciones de mediciones generales son equivalentes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before proceeding further, let's be more precise about the measurement, how "
"we're viewing it as a channel, and what assumptions we're making about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Antes de continuar, seamos más precisos: cuál es la medición, cómo la "
"concebimos como canal, y qué suposiciones hacemos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, we'll suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is the system to be measured, and that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m.$\n"
"We let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be the system that stores measurement outcomes, so its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ and we represent the measurement as a channel named $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Our assumption is that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is *classical* — which is to say that no matter what state we start with for $\\mathsf{X},$ the state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ we obtain is represented by a diagonal density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Como antes, suponemos que $\\mathsf{X}$ es el sistema a medir y que los posibles resultados de medición son los enteros $0,\\ldots,m-1$ para un entero positivo $m$.\n"
"Sea $\\mathsf{Y}$ el sistema que almacena los resultados de medición; su conjunto de estados clásicos es por tanto $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, y representamos la medición como un canal $\\Phi$ de $\\mathsf{X}$ a $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Nuestra suposición es que $\\mathsf{Y}$ es *clásico* — es decir, independientemente del estado en que se encuentre $\\mathsf{X}$ al inicio, el estado resultante de $\\mathsf{Y}$ siempre está representado por una matriz de densidad diagonal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can express in mathematical terms that the output of $\\Phi$ is always diagonal in the following way.\n"
"First define the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m$ on $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos expresar en términos matemáticos que la salida de $\\Phi$ es siempre diagonal de la siguiente manera.\n"
"Primero, definamos el canal completamente defasante $\\Delta_m$ sobre $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This channel is analogous to the completely dephasing qubit channel $\\Delta$ from the previous lesson.\n"
"As a linear mapping, it zeros out all of the off-diagonal entries of an input matrix and leaves the diagonal alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Este canal es análogo al canal completamente defasante de qubit $\\Delta$ de la lección anterior.\n"
"Como aplicación lineal, establece todas las entradas fuera de la diagonal de una matriz de entrada en cero y deja la diagonal sin cambios.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now, a simple way to express that a given density matrix $\\sigma$ is diagonal is by the equation\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma).$\n"
"In words, zeroing out all of the off-diagonal entries of a density matrix has no effect if and only if the off-diagonal entries were all zero to begin with.\n"
"The channel $\\Phi$ therefore satisfies our assumption — that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is classical — if and only if\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma simple de expresar que una matriz de densidad dada $\\sigma$ es diagonal es:\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma)$.\n"
"En otras palabras: poner a cero todas las entradas fuera de la diagonal de una matriz de densidad no tiene efecto si y solo si esas entradas eran todas cero desde el principio.\n"
"El canal $\\Phi$ satisface nuestra suposición — que $\\mathsf{Y}$ es clásico — si y solo si\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for every density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para toda matriz de densidad $\\rho$ que describe un estado de "
"$\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the formulations {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"
msgstr "Equivalencia de las formulaciones {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to matrices {#channels-to-matrices}"
msgstr "De canales a matrices {#channels-to-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$ with the "
"property that\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que tenemos un canal de $\\mathsf{X}$ a $\\mathsf{Y}$ con la "
"propiedad de que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every density matrix $\\rho.$\n"
"This may alternatively be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"para toda matriz de densidad $\\rho$.\n"
"Esto puede expresarse alternativamente como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Like all channels, we can express $\\Phi$ in Kraus form for some way of choosing Kraus matrices\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Como cualquier canal, podemos escribir $\\Phi$ en forma de Kraus para una elección adecuada de matrices de Kraus\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This provides us with an alternative expression for the diagonal entries of "
"$\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto nos proporciona una expresión alternativa para las entradas diagonales "
"de $\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "para\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, for these same matrices $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ we can express the "
"channel $\\Phi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para las mismas matrices $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$, el canal $\\Phi$ puede "
"expresarse como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression is consistent with our description of general measurements "
"in terms of matrices, as we see each measurement outcome appearing with "
"probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta expresión coincide con nuestra descripción de mediciones generales "
"mediante matrices: cada resultado de medición ocurre con probabilidad "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's observe that the two properties required of the collection of matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ to describe a general measurement are indeed satisfied.\n"
"The first property is that they're all positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"One way to see this is to observe that, for every vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ having entries in correspondence with the classical state of $\\mathsf{X}$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora verificamos que las dos propiedades que la colección de matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ debe satisfacer para una medición general se cumplen efectivamente.\n"
"La primera propiedad es que todas las matrices son positivas semidefinidas.\n"
"Esto se deduce del hecho de que para cualquier vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ con entradas correspondientes a los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ se tiene:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second property is that if we sum these matrices we get the identity "
"matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"La segunda propiedad es que la suma de estas matrices es la matriz "
"identidad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last equality follows from the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so its "
"Kraus matrices must satisfy this condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"La última igualdad se sigue del hecho de que $\\Phi$ es un canal y sus "
"matrices de Kraus deben satisfacer está condición.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices to channels {#matrices-to-channels}"
msgstr "De matrices a canales {#matrices-to-channels}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's verify that for any collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ of "
"positive semidefinite matrices satisfying $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},$ the mapping defined by\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora verificamos que para una colección arbitraria "
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ de matrices positivas semidefinidas que "
"satisfacen $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, la "
"aplicación definida por\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is indeed a valid channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr "es efectivamente un canal válido de $\\mathsf{X}$ a $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to do this is to compute the Choi representation of this mapping.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma de hacerlo es calcular la representación de Choi de esta "
"aplicación.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The transpose of each $P_a$ is introduced for the third equality because\n"
msgstr "La transpuesta de cada $P_a$ aparece en la tercera igualdad porque\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows for the expressions $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert$ and "
"$\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$ to appear, which simplify to the "
"identity matrix upon summing over $b$ and $c,$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto permite que aparezcan las expresiones $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b "
"\\vert$ y $\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$, que al sumar sobre $b$ y "
"$c$ respectivamente se simplifican a la matriz identidad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the assumption that $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ are positive semidefinite, so too are $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}.$\n"
"In particular, transposing a Hermitian matrix results in another Hermitian matrix, and the eigenvalues of any square matrix and its transpose always agree.\n"
"It follows that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite.\n"
"Tracing out the output system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (which is the system on the right) yields\n"
msgstr ""
"Dado que $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ son positivas semidefinidas por hipótesis, también lo son $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}$.\n"
"En particular, la transpuesta de una matriz hermítica es nuevamente una matriz hermítica, y los valores propios de una matriz cuadrada y su transpuesta siempre coinciden.\n"
"De esto se deduce que $J(\\Phi)$ es positiva semidefinida.\n"
"Tomar la traza parcial sobre el sistema de salida $\\mathsf{Y}$ (el sistema derecho) da\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and so we conclude that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
msgstr "y concluimos que $\\Phi$ es un canal.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Partial measurements {#partial-measurements}"
msgstr "Mediciones parciales {#partial-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have multiple systems that are collectively in a quantum state, and a general measurement is performed on one of the systems.\n"
"This results in one of the measurement outcomes, selected at random according to probabilities determined by the measurement and the state of the system prior to the measurement.\n"
"The resulting state of the remaining systems will then, in general, depend on which measurement outcome was obtained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que varios sistemas se encuentran juntos en un estado cuántico, y se realiza una medición general sobre uno de los sistemas.\n"
"Esto produce uno de los resultados de medición, elegido aleatoriamente con probabilidades determinadas por la medición y el estado del sistema antes de la medición.\n"
"El estado resultante de los sistemas restantes depende entonces, en general, de que resultado de medición se obtuvo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's examine how this works for a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ when the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured.\n"
"(We're naming the system on the right $\\mathsf{Z}$ because we'll take $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be a system representing the classical output of the measurement when we view it as a channel.)\n"
"We can then easily generalize to the situation in which the systems are swapped as well as to three or more systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Examinemos cómo funciona esto para un par de sistemas $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ cuando se mide el sistema $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"(Llamamos al sistema derecho $\\mathsf{Z}$ porque reservamos $\\mathsf{Y}$ para el sistema que representa la salida clásica de la medición cuando la consideramos como un canal.)\n"
"Posteriormente, esto se generaliza fácilmente al caso en que los sistemas están intercambiados o hay tres o más sistemas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ prior to the measurement is"
" described by a density matrix $\\rho,$ which we can write as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sea el estado de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ antes de la medición descrito "
"por una matriz de densidad $\\rho$, que podemos escribir como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this expression we're assuming the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are "
"$0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"En esta expresión suponemos que los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ son "
"$0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll assume that the measurement itself is described by the collection of matrices\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}.$\n"
"This measurement may alternatively be described as a channel $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y},$ where $\\mathsf{Y}$ is a new system having classical state set $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
"Specifically, the action of this channel can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Suponemos que la medición se describe mediante la colección de matrices\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$.\n"
"Esta medición puede describirse alternativamente como un canal $\\Phi$ de $\\mathsf{X}$ a $\\mathsf{Y}$, donde $\\mathsf{Y}$ es un nuevo sistema con conjunto de estados clásicos $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
"La acción de este canal puede expresarse concretamente como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Outcome probabilities {#outcome-probabilities}"
msgstr "Probabilidades de los resultados {#outcome-probabilities}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're considering a measurement of the system $\\mathsf{X},$ so the probabilities with which different measurement outcomes are obtained can depend only on $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}},$ the reduced state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"In particular, the probability for each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ to appear can be expressed in three equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dado que estamos considerando una medición del sistema $\\mathsf{X}$, las probabilidades de los distintos resultados de medición solo pueden depender del estado reducido $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}$ de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"En particular, la probabilidad de cada resultado $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ puede expresarse de tres formas equivalentes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first expression naturally represents the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ based on what we already know about measurements of a single system.\n"
"To get the second expression we're simply using the definition $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"La primera expresión representa la probabilidad del resultado $a$ de forma natural, basandose en lo que ya sabemos sobre mediciones en un solo sistema.\n"
"La segunda expresión se sigue directamente de la definición $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get the third expression requires more thought — and learners are encouraged to convince themselves that it is true.\n"
"Here's a hint: The equivalence between the second and third expressions does not depend on $\\rho$ being a density matrix or on each $P_a$ being positive semidefinite. Try showing it first for tensor products of the form $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ and then conclude that it must be true in general by linearity.\n"
msgstr ""
"La tercera expresión requiere un poco más de reflexion — y te invitamos a convencerte de que es verdadera.\n"
"Aquí hay una pista: la equivalencia entre la segunda y la tercera expresión no depende de que $\\rho$ sea una matriz de densidad o de que cada $P_a$ sea positiva semidefinida. Intenta demostrarlo primero para productos tensoriales de la forma $\\rho = M\\otimes N$, y luego concluye por linealidad para el caso general.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the equivalence of the first and third expressions in the previous equation may not be immediate, it does make sense.\n"
"Starting from a measurement on $\\mathsf{X},$ we're effectively defining a measurement of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z}),$ where we simply throw away $\\mathsf{Z}$ and measure $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Like all measurements, this new measurement can be described by a collection of matrices, and it's not surprising that this measurement is described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Aunque la equivalencia entre la primera y la tercera expresión no es inmediatamente obvia, resulta plausible.\n"
"Partiendo de una medición sobre $\\mathsf{X}$, definimos efectivamente una medición de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ en la que simplemente descartamos $\\mathsf{Z}$ y medimos $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Como cualquier medición, esta nueva medición puede describirse mediante una colección de matrices, y no es sorprendente que esta medición se describa mediante la colección\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States conditioned on measurement outcomes {#states-conditioned-on-"
"measurement-outcomes}"
msgstr ""
"Estados condicionados a los resultados de medición {#states-conditioned-on-"
"measurement-outcomes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we want to determine not only the probabilities for the different outcomes but also the resulting state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ conditioned on each measurement outcome, we can look to the channel description of the measurement.\n"
"In particular, let's examine the state we get when we apply $\\Phi$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ and do nothing to $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si deseamos determinar no solo las probabilidades de los distintos resultados, sino también el estado resultante de $\\mathsf{Z}$ condicionado a cada resultado de medición, podemos utilizar la descripción de la medición como canal.\n"
"En particular, consideramos el estado que obtenemos al aplicar $\\Phi$ a $\\mathsf{X}$ y dejar $\\mathsf{Z}$ sin cambios.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is a density matrix by virtue of the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so each matrix\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ is necessarily positive semidefinite.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una matriz de densidad, ya que $\\Phi$ es un canal; por tanto, cada matriz\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ es necesariamente positiva semidefinida.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One final step transforms this expression into one that reveals what we're "
"looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un último paso reescribe esta expresión en una forma que revela lo que "
"buscamos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is an example of a *classical-quantum state*,\n"
msgstr "Este es un ejemplo de un *estado clásico-cuántico*,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"like we saw in the *Density matrices* lesson.\n"
"For each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ we have with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"como los que conocimos en la lección sobre *matrices de densidad*.\n"
"Para cada resultado de medición $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ se cumple: con probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is in the classical state $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle a "
"\\vert$ and $\\mathsf{Z}$ is in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\mathsf{Y}$ se encuentra en el estado clásico $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle "
"a \\vert$ y $\\mathsf{Z}$ en el estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "That is, this is the density matrix we obtain by normalizing\n"
msgstr "Esta es la matriz de densidad que obtenemos normalizando\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"by dividing it by its trace.\n"
"(Formally speaking, the state $\\sigma_a$ is only defined when the probability $p(a)$ is nonzero;\n"
"when $p(a) = 0$ this state is irrelevant, for it refers to a discrete event that occurs with probability zero.)\n"
msgstr ""
"dividiendo por su traza.\n"
"(Formalmente, el estado $\\sigma_a$ solo está definido cuando la probabilidad $p(a)$ es distinta de cero; si $p(a) = 0$, este estado es irrelevante, ya que se refiere a un evento discreto con probabilidad cero.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Naturally, the outcome probabilities are consistent with our previous "
"observations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naturalmente, las probabilidades de los resultados son consistentes con "
"nuestras observaciones anteriores.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In summary, this is what happens when the measurement "
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on $\\mathsf{X}$ when "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ is in the state $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"En resumen, cuando se realiza la medición $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ sobre "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ mientras $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ se encuentra en el estado"
" $\\rho$:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each outcome $a$ appears with probability $p(a) = "
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada resultado $a$ ocurre con probabilidad $p(a) = "
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a,$ the state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ is then"
" represented by the density matrix $\\sigma_a$ shown in the equation $(2),$ "
"which is obtained by normalizing "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Condicionado al resultado $a$, el estado de $\\mathsf{Z}$ viene dado por la "
"matriz de densidad $\\sigma_a$ de la ecuación $(2)$, obtenida normalizando "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalization {#generalization}"
msgstr "Generalización {#generalization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can adapt this description to other situations, such as when the ordering of the systems is reversed or when there are three or more systems.\n"
"Conceptually it is straightforward, although it can become cumbersome to write down the formulas.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta descripción puede adaptarse a otras situaciones, como cuando el orden de los sistemas está invertido o cuando hay tres o más sistemas.\n"
"Conceptualmente es sencillo, aunque las fórmulas pueden volverse engorrosas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, if we have $r$ systems $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r,$ "
"the state of the compound system $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is "
"$\\rho,$ and the measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on "
"$\\mathsf{X}_k$, the following happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"En general, si tenemos $r$ sistemas $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r$, "
"el estado del sistema compuesto $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ es "
"$\\rho$, y se realiza la medición $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ sobre "
"$\\mathsf{X}_k$, se cumple lo siguiente.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each outcome $a$ appears with probability\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada resultado $a$ ocurre con probabilidad\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a,$ the state of $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is then represented by the following density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Condicionado al resultado $a$, el estado de $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ viene dado por la siguiente matriz de densidad:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
